l scope; store provider, endpoint, model, acquired/refreshed/expires timestamps; refresh on reuse; expire abandoned leases; invalidate leases when endpoint disappears, stops advertising the model, or enters cooldown. Role remains observational; validated CorrelationID is the first sticky key source unless a more specific worker/session key already exists. Out of scope: provider utilization probes, route scoring with utilization, route-status UI, and distributed/shared lease backend.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. go test ./internal/routing ./... -run \u0026#39;Sticky|Lease|Routing\u0026#39; passes. 2. Same sticky key repeatedly returns the same provider endpoint while the lease is live and endpoint remains eligible. 3. Expired sticky key is assigned fresh. 4. Removed, unavailable, or model-mismatched endpoint invalidates the lease and records an invalidation reason. 5. Different sticky keys can hold different endpoint leases concurrently without data races.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:routing, kind:feature\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-c58969b6\" spec-id=\"FEAT-004\" base-rev=\"3b8eccff1e238b39065813d35fd3efd6b71b0a18\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260506T011608-765fc81f\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"FEAT-004\" path=\"docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-004-model-routing.md\"\u003eFeature Specification: FEAT-004 — Shared Model Catalog, Power-Based Routing, and Provider Configuration\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260506T011608-765fc81f","base_rev":"3b8eccff1e238b39065813d35fd3efd6b71b0a18","bead_id":"fizeau-dac696fc","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260506T011608-765fc81f","correlation_id":"fizeau-dac696fc:20260506T011608-765fc81f","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260506T011608-765fc81f/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"3abffc035865c02f63f29fada2abdbb246a4dee5307cee7374442612d4309f7c